the picker has one row for each model of each head in the door
the picker's rows are in splice.toml's order of heads
a row's model is the ID its head's own /v1/models lists
a row's label is the model's own label
a row's description names splice and its head's command
splice desktop --json lists the same models as the picker
each model splice desktop --json lists has its model, label, head and command
a head that forwards the caller's own Claude login has no row
left_out names the head that forwards the caller's own Claude login, with that reason
splice desktop names the head that forwards the caller's own Claude login
a head whose login is missing has no row
left_out names the head whose login is missing
splice desktop names the head whose login is missing with the command that signs it in
a head signed in again is in the picker with no command run
a head signed in again is no longer left out
the door and its key stay as the file held them when the lineup changes
a head added to splice is in the picker with no command run
the picker keeps splice.toml's order of heads when a head is added
a model of a head that was added runs through the door the file held before
a head removed from splice leaves the picker
a removed head's selectors are refused
a head whose login is removed leaves the picker
